DTEND:20270315T163000Z
SUMMARY:[Reviewer] Snapshot: Optional - join the 2027 annual review
DESCRIPTION:Responsible: Reviewer (external reviewer)\n\nVideo call\; the o
 ne time each year the scored rules may change. Comments welcome beforehand
 .\n\nSource: docs/schedule/schedule.yaml
CATEGORIES:External reviewer
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:reviewer-packet@2027-04-02@internet-security-snapshot
DTSTAMP:20261024T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270402
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270403
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
SUMMARY:[Claude] Snapshot: Send the reviewer the Q1 2027 review packet
DESCRIPTION:Responsible: Claude (claude)\n\nOnce the provisional Q1 2027 re
 port is approved: links to the report\, the registered plan\, prereg/DEVIA
 TIONS.md\, the data bundle and the exact code commit\; the sample of hand 
 decisions with their rules\; a short review template (holds up / doesn't /
  would change).\n\nSource: docs/schedule/schedule.yaml
CATEGORIES:Claude
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:external-review@2027-04-03@internet-security-snapshot
DTSTAMP:20261024T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270403
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270429
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
SUMMARY:[Reviewer] Snapshot: Independent review of the Q1 2027 provisional 
 report
DESCRIPTION:Responsible: Reviewer (external reviewer)\n\nAbout 8-12 hours. 
 Read the provisional Q1 2027 report against the registered plan and the de
 viations log\; check that each headline figure is computed as the plan def
 ines it (read the code\, or recompute a few numbers from the data bundle)\
 ; look at the sample of hand decisions and their written rules. Send a sho
 rt written review (two to five pages: what holds up\, what doesn't\, what 
 you'd change) by 28 April. The window can move a week or two if needed\; p
 ublication is 1 May.\n\nSource: docs/schedule/schedule.yaml
CATEGORIES:External reviewer
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:reviewer-check-in@2027-04-15@internet-security-snapshot
DTSTAMP:20261024T000000Z
DTSTART:20270415T140000Z
DTEND:20270415T143000Z
SUMMARY:[Paul] Snapshot: Optional mid-review check-in with the reviewer
DESCRIPTION:Responsible: Paul (author)\n\nAnswer questions\; confirm the re
 view will arrive by 28 April or agree a new date.\n\nSource: docs/schedule
 /schedule.yaml
CATEGORIES:Author
END:VEVENT
